Vocab-truncated draft head for Qwen3.5/3.8 MTP speculative decoding.

If the model directory contains mtp_draft_vocab_ids.pt and the checkpoint has
mtp.draft_lm_head.* tensors (both produced by prepare/build_draft_vocab.py), the MTP
drafter scores only those rows instead of the full 248k-row lm_head; logits of
all other ids are -inf. Speculative decoding stays exact (rejection sampling
uses the target model), only the acceptance rate can change. Set
MTP_DRAFT_VOCAB=0 to fall back to the shared full lm_head.

GPTQ qweight is [K/pack, V]. VocabParallelEmbedding.weight_loader pads and copies
along dim 0 (unquantized [V, H]). A draft vocab that is not a multiple of
DEFAULT_VOCAB_PADDING_SIZE (64) — 40968 after pack=4 alignment — is allocated as
41024 and load crashes (41024 vs 40968 on dim 1). Allocate the head at the padded
width and right-pad the checkpoint tensors so Marlin N stays 64-aligned. Existing
40968-row heads load without a rebuild.

Apply from the installed vllm package directory:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/qwen3_5-mtp-draft-vocab.patch

Validated against vLLM 0.28.0.

